  "separation_rules": [
    "National data have no row-level patient, event, hospital or procedure linkage to California reports. Keep them in separate tables.",
    "National SSI totals may include California; never add national SSI events or pathogen reports to the 72,854 reports, 6,737,972 operations and 37,525 California SSIs.",
    "All-surgery rows, SSI-depth rows and surgical category rows are overlapping summaries. Use a declared view before aggregating.",
    "Blank source values are unavailable or suppressed, not zero. Exact tested counts cannot be inferred uniquely from rounded percentages.",
    "Original non-SSI bloodstream Data/Pathogens.csv, Resistance.csv and Clinical_sensitivity.csv are a separate evidence inventory, not used to establish the California SSI sample or the national SSI source-cell analyses."
  ]
